From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/50] ASoC: sm8150: prepare the DP codec DAI before starting
 the AFE port

Playback to DisplayPort is expected to fail with

  qcom-q6afe: AFE enable for port 0x6020 failed -110

ASoC prepares a link's CPU DAIs before its codec DAIs: snd_soc_pcm_dai_prepare()
walks rtd->dais, and that array holds the CPU DAIs first.  On this link the
CPU DAI is q6afe, whose prepare calls q6afe_port_start() for AFE port 0x6020
(AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX), and the codec DAI is the DP controller's
hdmi-codec.  Its prepare is the only hook that reaches msm_dp_audio_prepare(),
which programs SDP and ACR and enables the DP audio engine: the DRM HDMI audio
callbacks (struct drm_connector_hdmi_audio_funcs) have startup, prepare,
shutdown and mute_stream, but no hw_params, so nothing turns DP audio on
earlier.  The DSP is therefore asked to start a port whose sink is still off.

The downstream 4.14 reference kernel for this device ran the other way:
soc_pcm_prepare() prepared the codec DAIs before the CPU DAI, so the
msm-ext-disp codec enabled DP audio before msm-dai-q6-hdmi started the port.
That ordering is read from the LineageOS lineage-23.2 tree
(sound/soc/soc-pcm.c:775-830, fetched read-only; excerpts in
docs/reference/lineage-23.2-dp-audio-evidence.md).  It is the downstream
reference tree, not proven to be the factory build, so it establishes what
downstream code does, not what the shipped image executed.

The link's prepare runs before either DAI's, so prepare the codec DAIs from
there for DISPLAY_PORT_RX.  The core prepares them again after the CPU DAI.

Experiment, not a proven fix; it is only reachable when the DisplayPort audio
link is enabled (the dts patch ships it disabled), so without that one-line DT
change this patch is inert.  Whether the ordering is the cause of the -110
timeout is untested; only the ordering difference itself is established from
source.

Side effects, checked:

 - snd_soc_dai_prepare() performs no ASoC bookkeeping.  It checks
   snd_soc_dai_stream_valid(), calls ops->prepare and logs the error
   (sound/soc/soc-dai.c); the rollback marks (soc_dai_mark_*) exist only for
   hw_params, startup, trigger and compress startup, so calling prepare out of
   band cannot unbalance the startup/shutdown symmetry.

 - Repeating the codec prepare is allowed by contract: the DRM HDMI audio
   prepare callback is documented as "Can be called multiple times for each
   setup" (include/drm/drm_connector.h) and hdmi_codec_prepare() has no state
   of its own.  msm_dp_audio_prepare() re-programs SDP/ACR/exit level, sets
   MMSS_DP_AUDIO_CFG bit 0 again (idempotent read-modify-write), re-arms
   dp->audio_comp through msm_dp_display_signal_audio_start() and sets
   audio_enabled = true.

 - The completion is the one non-idempotent detail.  It is completed by
   msm_dp_audio_shutdown() (PCM close -> hdmi_codec_shutdown) and waited on
   only by msm_dp_display_disable() with a 5 second timeout.  Two re-arms in a
   row before any waiter are equivalent to one.  The remaining window is an
   unplug racing the microseconds between the link prepare and the core's
   codec prepare: the wait would then end at its existing 5s timeout with
   "audio comp timeout" instead of being woken early.  That is bounded, logged
   by the DP driver, and clears audio_enabled afterwards; it does not corrupt
   state.

 - If the codec prepare succeeds and the CPU prepare then fails (-110), the
   codec is left enabled until the PCM is closed; close runs the DAI shutdown
   (soc_pcm_clean() -> snd_soc_dai_shutdown(), reverse order), which calls
   msm_dp_audio_shutdown() and completes the completion.  No stuck state.

Signed-off-by: Nura rc4 displayport series <rc4-displayport@nura.invalid>
Nura-Category: local-workaround
Nura-Origin: nura rc4 displayport series (LineageOS 23.2 reference)
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
index 459f7ea..40da738 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
@@ -386,6 +386,43 @@ static int sm8150_snd_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 	struct sdw_stream_runtime *sruntime = data->sruntime[cpu_dai->id];
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * ASoC prepares a link's CPU DAIs before its codec DAIs
+	 * (snd_soc_pcm_dai_prepare() walks rtd->dais, CPUs first).  For
+	 * DisplayPort the CPU DAI is q6afe, whose prepare starts AFE port
+	 * 0x6020 (AFE_PORT_ID_HDMI_OVER_DP_RX), and the codec DAI is the DP
+	 * controller's hdmi-codec, whose prepare is the only hook that turns
+	 * the DP audio engine on: msm_dp_audio_prepare() programs the SDP and
+	 * ACR blocks and enables the audio engine, and the DRM HDMI audio
+	 * callbacks that forward to it have no hw_params op.
+	 *
+	 * So by default the DSP is asked to start the DP audio port before the
+	 * DP side of it is enabled.  The downstream 4.14 reference kernel
+	 * prepared the codec DAIs first; do the same here, before the core
+	 * prepares the CPU DAI, to get that order back.
+	 *
+	 * The core prepares the codec DAIs again afterwards.  That is safe: the
+	 * DRM HDMI audio prepare is documented as callable repeatedly,
+	 * msm_dp_audio_prepare() only re-programs SDP/ACR/exit level and re-arms
+	 * its completion, and no waiter can observe the intermediate state
+	 * except a concurrent unplug, which then finishes on its existing 5s
+	 * timeout.  It returns -EINVAL while DP is not powered, i.e. while the
+	 * display is unplugged, which aborts the prepare as it would have done
+	 * later.
+	 */
+	if (cpu_dai->id == DISPLAY_PORT_RX) {
+		struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai;
+		int i;
+
+		for_each_rtd_codec_dais(rtd, i, codec_dai) {
+			ret = snd_soc_dai_prepare(codec_dai, substream);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!sruntime)
 		return 0;
 
-- 
